d — it now seeds `currentBranchErr` (instead of `currentBranch`) and asserts `state.resolve()` returns success with `AllBranches=true`. This is the exact \"`isLocal() && !AllBranches`\" gate check review-03 requested.\n25\t  - **Local + current branch + detached HEAD → clean error at `state.resolve()`**: Not explicitly covered by a dedicated new test. `TestRunDispatchWizard_FailsEarlyWhenCurrentBranchCannotBeResolved` only asserts the wizard bootstrap no longer fails early (\"run dispatch wizard\" wraps the form-execution error in `t.Chdir` mode without a TTY); it does not drive `state.resolve()` in `modeChoice=Local` + `localBranchMode=Current` + `currentBranchErr≠nil`. See Suggestion below. The logic is correct on inspection (default state hits the gate), but the third permutation is not regression-pinned.\n26\t\n27\t- [x] **Important #2 — `resolveRepoFullName` drops underlying error context.** **Fixed** by `ae819d10c`. Both error branches now `logging.Warn(ctx, ..., \"error\", err)` with a `\"step\"` attr (`origin_remote` / `parse_origin_remote`) and wrap the underlying error via `%w` in the returned `fmt.Errorf` ([mode_local.go:302-315](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go:302)). The middle case (`len(URLs) == 0`) stays as `errors.New` — correct, since there's no underlying error. Callers updated: `mode_cloud.go:65`, `mode_local.go:132`, plus the signature change to thread `ctx`. No test files referenced the old signature.\n28\t\n29\t## New Findings\n30\t\n31\t### High\n32\t\n33\tNone.\n34\t\n35\t### Important (Should Fix)\n36\t\n37\tNone.\n38\t\n39\t### Suggestions (Consider)\n40\t\n41\t- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard_test.go:341](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard_test.go:341) — `TestRunDispatchWizard_FailsEarlyWhenCurrentBranchCannotBeResolved` is now stale-named.** The test asserts the opposite of what its name implies — it now verifies the wizard does **not** fail early and instead proceeds to form execution (which errors as \"run dispatch wizard\" on a no